    "md5": "fde4a9c35e7440d9ba98f6053f5ed168",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1200,
    "chunk_text": "Revisiting the existing Electricity Act No.36 of 2024\n\nPress briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)\n\n- An Expert Committee has been appointed by the Secretary to the Ministry of Energy with the approval of the Cabinet to obtain appropriate recommendations for amending the Electricity Act No. 36 of 2024. The said Committee has taken measures to seek the views of the key stakeholders of the power sector. Accordingly, actions have been taken to conduct knowledge sharing sessions and obtain written views and proposals and thus, 59 stakeholders have submitted their written views and proposals. In addition, views have been obtained from development partners who provide funds for development projects in the power sector as well as from other parties interested in restructuring the power sector. Taking into account the said views and proposals, the Expert Committee has submitted its final Report containing the proposed amendments to the Electricity Act No. 36 of 2024. The proposal made by the Minister of Energy to prepare a Bill to amend the Electricity Act, based on the recommendations in the said Report, was approved by the Cabinet."
